WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.152
Veterans offered MAID.

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:04.261
The documented cases.

00:00:04.261 --> 00:00:11.113
They called Veterans Affairs Canada seeking help for PTSD, depression, chronic pain, and service-related trauma.

00:00:11.113 --> 00:00:14.125
They were offered medical assistance in dying.

00:00:14.125 --> 00:00:18.704
At least four confirmed cases have been documented in parliamentary testimony.

00:00:18.704 --> 00:00:20.931
The veterans were not dying.

00:00:20.931 --> 00:00:28.772
They were suffering from conditions created by their military service — service to the same country whose government now offered them death instead of treatment.

00:00:28.772 --> 00:00:37.840
This page documents the confirmed cases from parliamentary committee records, the systemic context that produced them, and the intersection with the immigration to MAID pipeline.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.352
When the system treats its own veterans this way, no immigrant is safe.

00:00:42.352 --> 00:00:46.943
Documented cases of veterans offered MAID instead of mental health treatment.

00:00:46.943 --> 00:00:49.624
From parliamentary committee testimony.

00:00:49.624 --> 00:00:54.249
How the veteran MAID cases connect to the broader institutional capture architecture.

00:00:54.249 --> 00:00:56.272
The ultimate betrayal.

00:00:56.272 --> 00:01:03.113
If a country will offer death to its own veterans — the people who risked their lives in its service — it will offer death to anyone.

00:01:03.113 --> 00:01:08.227
The veteran MAID cases are the most visceral proof of the pipeline documented across this site.

00:01:08.227 --> 00:01:11.193
Immigrants arrive with credentials that are denied.

00:01:11.193 --> 00:01:14.045
Their health deteriorates over a decade.

00:01:14.045 --> 00:01:16.477
They become eligible for MAID.

00:01:16.477 --> 00:01:18.636
Veterans serve with honour.

00:01:18.636 --> 00:01:20.988
Their service creates trauma.

00:01:20.988 --> 00:01:23.579
The system fails to treat the trauma.

00:01:23.579 --> 00:01:25.511
They are offered MAID.

00:01:25.511 --> 00:01:32.284
Both pipelines end at the same place: a death that saves the system money and benefits the PM's financial holdings.

00:01:32.284 --> 00:01:35.647
This is not a failure of individual employees.

00:01:35.647 --> 00:01:41.715
It is the documented output of institutional architecture that values fiscal efficiency over human life.
